                <pb facs="0764" n="666" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg666"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/2846: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-03T10:00:00-05:00">October 3, 1930—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:30 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>120. Student’s funeral passed off quietly. There is no sign of further
                    disturbances. Congress meets this afternoon to act on President’s message
                    requesting authorization to suspend Constitutional guarantees not only in
                    Habana, as previously reported, but anywhere in the country.</p>
                <p>Press censorship actually although not officially declared.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
